  "notes": "PLAT-01 cycle 3: phenomenon A, the sustained burst at roughly 10 ms spacing across all isolated cores. Not a figure. Last cycle of the D-20 budget. Break limit 200 us, which is T_A derived in cycle 1 from a traced baseline and recorded in docs/rig/plat01-stall-investigation.md. Target is the roughly 1.2 second burst observed inside a 10 minute run on 2026-08-28. Cycle 2 ran 90 minutes at T_B 3000 us and phenomenon B did not reproduce, maximum 72 us; this cycle adds two hours of exposure and is expected not to fire, since 200 us is more than twice any maximum this rig has produced on a clean run. A cycle that fires nothing is exposure and is committed anyway. Instrument ordering: (a) sequential, two separate runs, NOT (b) concurrent. (b) would run rtla sampling threads at SCHED_FIFO on cpus 6-11, the same cores this run measures at priority 99, which is what starved 2026-09-06-precision3591-screen-02, and an investigation run records TracersQuiescent NotApplicable so nothing would refuse it. Event set armed by scripts/nr-arm-trace.sh: sched:sched_switch sched:sched_wakeup irq:irq_handler_entry irq:irq_handler_exit timer:hrtimer_expire_entry workqueue:workqueue_execute_start ipi:ipi_send_cpu ipi:ipi_send_cpumask tlb:tlb_flush. tracing_cpumask 3fffff over all 22 logical cpus so an IPI sender is visible and not only its arrival; buffer_size_kb 8195 per cpu. Whether the break fired, and the buffer line counts if it did, are recorded in the plan summary rather than here: this note is written at launch."
